AccountV3PolicyStorage
├── given a canonical policy
│   ├── when one to sixteen active mixed signers are stored
│   │   └── it should preserve ABI bytes, signer IDs, roles, delays and policy hash
│   ├── when address keys use their highest bits
│   │   └── it should reconstruct all twenty bytes without duplicating storage
│   └── when a long WebAuthn key is replaced or the array shrinks
│       └── it should erase dynamic words and never resurrect old authority
├── given a malformed policy or ambiguous descriptor
│   └── it should revert without changing existing policy or adjacent state
├── given a stored tagged union
│   ├── inactive variant words should never affect authority
│   └── an unknown kind should fail closed
└── given a packed persistent creation window
    ├── it should reproduce the exact ERC-4337 validation data
    ├── it should survive unrelated packed-header writes
    └── consuming it should preserve flags, version, policy and all other state
